title: whoami prints '(local session alias — not a relay registration)' for aliases that ARE relay-registered
updated_at: "2026-07-17T16:57:13Z"
---
During cross-host dogfood (2026-07-18): 'c2c whoami --relay' for kimi-suvi-lumo-9cr1 printed 'alias: kimi-suvi-lumo-9cr1 (local session alias — not a relay registration)' while the same alias was simultaneously alive/registered on the relay (visible in 'c2c relay list' and able to 'relay register' + 'relay dm poll'). The parenthetical misleads operators into re-registering or thinking relay is unset. The check behind that note appears to test something narrower (lease in connector state?) than actual relay registration.